 "title": "Owen County Auditor | Financial Records &amp; Reports",
 "text": "Owen County Auditor | Financial Records & Reports\nSkip to content ⚠ Owen County Travel Status: Yellow – Advisory. Use caution; routine travel may be restricted in hazardous areas. | 211 is now active for Owen County residents to report storm damage.\n✕\nOwen County Government\nOfficial Website of Owen County, Indiana\nSearch\nMain Menu Main Menu\nHome\nAbout Owen County\nLegal & Policies\nADA Statement\nPrivacy Policy\nPublic Records Request\nTitle VI Statement\nLocal Attractions\nNews & Updates\nGovernment\nCounty Directory\nElection Board & Voter Registration\nOrdinances & Resolutions\nRedevelopment Commission\nDepartments\nAuditor\nAddressing\nAssessor\nBuilding & Planning\nCASA\nCircuit Court I\nCircuit Court II\nClerk\nCommissioners\nCoroner\nCouncil\nCourt Services\nGIS & Mapping\nHealth Department\nHighway Department\nMaintenance\nProsecutor\nRecorder\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nVeteran Services\nPublic Safety & Emergency Services\n911 Communications Center\nEMS\nOCEMS Employment Application\nOCEMS History\nEMS FAQs\nIn Memory\nNotice of Privacy Practices\nSafe Sleep Program\nRescue\nEMA\nSecurity Center\nSheriff’s Office\nPublic Services\nEmployment Opportunities\nPermits & Licensing\nProperty Taxes\nSoil & Water\nCalendar & Events\nContact\nHome » Departments » Auditor\nAuditor\nThe County Auditor is the chief financial officer for Owen County. The Auditor oversees the accounting of all county funds, processes payroll for county employees, manages disbursements, and prepares key financial reports for public review and state compliance.\nKey Responsibilities\nMaintain county financial records\nProcess accounts payable and payroll\nDistribute property tax revenues to local units\nAssist with the annual budget process\nPrepare and submit state-required reports\nCommon Resources\nAuditor Forms\nOrdinances & Resolutions\nProperty Tax Info\nCONTRACTS\nPeters Municipal Consultants\nMeet the Auditor\nSheila Reeves\nOwen County Auditor\nsheila.reeves@owencounty.in.gov\n(812) 829-5000\nContact & Location\nOwen County Courthouse\n60 S. Main Street, Room 201\nSpencer, IN 47460\nOffice Hours:\nMonday–Friday, 8:00 AM – 4:00 PM\n2025 Certified Budget Order\nThe Indiana Department of Local Government Finance (DLGF) publishes official budget orders, levy limits, and property tax rates for each county. This includes the 2025 Budget Order, assessed value reports, and other key tax documents affecting local government funding and property tax rates.\nView the most recent certified budget documents for Owen County:\nView DLGF Portal\n2026 Upcoming Tax Sale\nThe public auction will be conducted as an electronic sale under IC 6-1.1-24-2(b)10. Each property will have its specific closing time posted on the auction website.\nOwe delinquent taxes on a property in this sale?\nPay the full amount owed by 4:00 PM local time, Tuesday, October 6, 2026 to keep your property out of the auction. Payment must be cash or certified funds, payable to the Owen County Treasurer, and delivered to: Owen County Treasurer, 60 South Main Street, Room 102A, Spencer, IN 47460.\nPlatform: www.zeusauction.com\nRegistration Opens: 09/05/2026\nRegistration Closes: 10/05/2026\nAuction Opens: 10/07/2026 at 10:00 AM (Local Time)\nCommence Closing: 10/07/2026 at 12:00 PM (Local Time)\nGo to Zeus Auction\nDownload 2026 Tax Sale Ad (PDF)\nThe full list of 141 properties, minimum bids, and parcel numbers is in the PDF above. Need it in an alternative format? Contact the Auditor’s office at (812) 829-5000.\nPage Last Updated\nSeptember 2, 2026\nContact Us\nOwen County Courthouse\n60 S. Main Street\nSpencer, IN 47460\nAuditor’s Office\n(812) 829-5000\nHours of Operation\nMonday – Friday: 8:00 AM to 4:00 PM\nClosed 12:00 PM – 1:00 PM for lunch\nClosed on weekends & federal holidays\nConnect With Us\nFacebook\nYouTube\nQuick Links\nDepartments\nCourt Services\nGovernment\nCalendar & Events\nPublic Records Request\nEmployment\nOwen County is a proud member of the Association of Indiana Counties and the National Association of Counties, working collaboratively to strengthen local governance and community services at both the state and national levels.\n© 2026 Owen County, Indiana. All rights reserved.\nPrivacy Policy | Accessibility Statement | Legal Center | Login\nWebsite Design & Site Management by David Martin Design LLC .",
